<%# The card intro modal — a creator-written pop-up shown OVER the card it
    explains, the first time a respondent lands on it.

    One partial, two modes, for the same reason _card_component is one: the
    editor's job is to show the creator the thing the respondent will meet, so
    the editor's version is the player's version plus contenteditable and a
    chrome strip. A second implementation would drift, and the drift would be
    invisible until a respondent saw it.

    Locals:
      card           — the card hash, PRIMARY language (rich_card_text needs it
                       to decide whether the stored html still describes the
                       string being shown)
      display        — the same card in the display language; defaults to card
      mode           — :editor or :player
      display_locale — the language the respondent is reading

    In :editor mode the partial renders whenever the modal EDITOR IS OPEN,
    which includes "open but empty" — a creator who has just clicked Add modal
    and typed nothing. Nothing is stored for that state (presence of the words
    IS the modal — Survey.sanitize_cards_images!), so the empty shell is
    editor-only chrome and never reaches a respondent. %>
<%
  mode           ||= :player
  display        ||= card
  display_locale   = (defined?(display_locale) && display_locale.presence) || SupportedLocales::DEFAULT
  editable         = (mode == :editor)
  ce_attr          = editable ? 'contenteditable="true"'.html_safe : "".html_safe
  modal_title      = display["modal_title"].to_s
%>
<%# Folded on arrival, in the editor only. Unfolded it covers the card — which
    is the truth about what a respondent sees, and exactly wrong for a creator
    who is still writing the question underneath it. So the replica opens to a
    slim bar carrying the modal's heading, and expands to the real thing on a
    click (or the moment the rail control adds one). %>
<div class="card-modal-layer<%= " is-editing is-folded" if editable %>"
     data-role="card-modal"
     <%= "hidden".html_safe unless editable %>
     role="dialog" aria-modal="true"
     aria-label="<%= t("card.modal_aria", locale: display_locale, default: "About this question") %>">
  <div class="card-modal-panel">
    <% if editable %>
      <%# Editor-only chrome. It names what this is and when it appears,
          because an unlabelled panel floating over a card in the feed reads
          as a card rather than as something that happens at play time — and
          folded it is the whole control, so the label doubles as a preview of
          the heading the creator wrote. %>
      <div class="card-modal-chrome">
        <button type="button" class="card-modal-fold"
                aria-expanded="false"
                title="<%= t("editor.modal_expand") %>"
                data-action="click->survey-editor#toggleCardModalFold">
          <%= card_modal_icon(14) %>
          <span class="card-modal-chrome-label" data-role="card-modal-chrome-label"><%= t("editor.modal_chrome") %></span>
          <span class="card-modal-fold-chevron" aria-hidden="true">▾</span>
        </button>
        <button type="button" class="card-modal-remove"
                title="<%= t("editor.modal_remove_title") %>"
                data-action="click->survey-editor#removeCardModal"><%= t("editor.modal_remove") %></button>
      </div>
    <% end %>

    <div class="card-modal-main">
      <%# The title is optional: a modal that is one short paragraph needs no
          heading, and an empty node would still take its line-height. In the
          editor it is always present (the placeholder fills it); for a
          respondent it renders only when it has words. %>
      <% if editable || modal_title.present? %>
        <div class="card-modal-title<%= " gate-placeholder" if editable %>"
             <%= ce_attr %>
             <% if editable %>data-role="card-modal-title"
                data-default-text="<%= t("editor.modal_title_placeholder") %>"<% end %>><%= modal_title %></div>
      <% end %>

      <%# Rich text on the body only — the title is one line, and no other
          single-line field in the app carries a formatting layer either. %>
      <div class="card-modal-text<%= " gate-placeholder" if editable %>"
           <%= ce_attr %>
           <% if editable %>data-role="card-modal-body" data-rich-text
              data-default-text="<%= t("editor.modal_body_placeholder") %>"<% end %>><%= rich_card_text(card, display, "modal_body") %></div>
    </div>

    <%# The dismiss button is PLATFORM copy, not the creator's. It reads "Got
        it" in the respondent's own language in all 26 of them, which a
        creator-typed word could only be in the ones they speak. Inert in the
        editor (tabindex -1, no action) so the replica can't be "pressed". %>
    <button type="button" class="card-modal-cta"
            <%= 'tabindex="-1"'.html_safe if editable %>
            <%= 'data-action="click->player#dismissCardModal"'.html_safe unless editable %>>
      <%= t("player.modal_continue", locale: display_locale, default: "Got it") %>
    </button>
  </div>
</div>
